<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>HTML Image Example</title>
</head>
<body>
  <h2>HTML Image Example</h2>
  <!-- The (img) tag embeds an image -->
  <!-- Attributes used: src (image URL), alt (alternate text), width and height -->

  <img src="https://www.shutterstock.com/image-photo/sun-sets-behind-mountain-ranges-600nw-2479236003.jpg" alt="Placeholder Image" width="150" height="150" />

  <p>
    The (img) tag inserts an image into the webpage.<br />
    Use the (src) attribute to specify the image URL.<br />
    Use the (alt) attribute to provide alternate text if the image cannot load while explaing the image .<br />
    You can also specify size using (width) and (height) attributes.
  </p>
</body>
</html>
